46:ADR-023 and ADR-024 narrow *when* evidence is owed, not *whether*. Three rounds
47-of pinned-source analysis showed that the original full-fidelity M0 contract
48-required semantics no public SSH library exposes, so every candidate needed
49-open-ended fork surgery before any client could run. Splitting the contract into
50-a viability tier and an evidence-gated M3 tier restores a working macOS client
51-path without weakening host-key-before-auth, Keychain-only secrets, fail-closed
52-DNS, bounded memory, the public PacketFlow bridge, the rootless exec/stdio
53-relay, or the signed/notarized release requirements.
